        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The contrasting business models of nonprofit and for-profit institutions of higher education are examined in this study. Faculty costs and the use of online technologies in instruction are shown to be treated very differently between the two models. A proposal for blending both models to realize the benefits of each will be developed from this study.",
