        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "✓ In this study, we examine the contrasting business models of nonprofit and for-profit institutions of higher education. The two models, we show, differ greatly in how they treat faculty costs and the use of online technologies in instruction. We will develop from this study a proposal for blending the benefits of both models to realize the benefits of each.",
